pe":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"measure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" each child, then ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"render"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" them with allocated sizes. This approach enables features like flexible spacers, proportional sizing, and proper alignment.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Two-Passes","text":"The Two Passes","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"anchor":"Pass-1-Measure","text":"Pass 1: Measure","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The parent proposes a size to each child via ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProposedSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each child responds with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ViewSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that describes how much space it needs and whether it can flex.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["Parent (VStack)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Text    → ViewSize(10, 1, flexible: false)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Spacer  → ViewSize(0, 0, flexible: true)","  └─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Button  → ViewSize(12, 1, flexible: false)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Pass-2-Render","text":"Pass 2: Render","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After measuring all children, the parent distributes the remaining space among flexible children and renders each child with its final allocated size.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["Parent allocates:","  Text   → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height","  Spacer → render(width: 40, height: 8)   \/\/ Gets remaining vertical space","  Button → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"ProposedSize","text":"ProposedSize","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProposedSize"},{"type":"text","text":" represents the space a parent offers to a child. Either dimension can 